## VCO-Managed Files

This project's `.claude/hooks/`, `.claude/scripts/`, `.claude/agents/`, `.claude/skills/`, and `.claude/settings.json` are shipped by VCO (the orchestrator). To update them, use the launcher (this project's Settings page → **Update bundle**, or the Projects page → **⟳ Update all** for every project) or run from the orchestrator root:

```bash
python -m vco_lib.project_init install-bundle \
  --folder '{{PROJECT_ROOT}}' \
  --orchestrator-root "$VCT_ORCHESTRATOR_ROOT" \
  --update
```

A shipped file you have edited locally is **adopted** on update: your bytes are backed up to `.claude/backups/bundle-adoptions/<timestamp>/` and the shipped version is written (`--force` does the same without the backup). Do not edit shipped files to change behaviour — disable the item from the launcher's per-project tabs instead. The one exception is `knowledge/**`: your KG nodes are your data and are always preserved, `--force` included. Files VCO could not adopt (backup failed) are listed in `.claude/.vco-manifest.json` under `preserved_files` and in `UPDATE_DEFERRED.md`.

## Moving this project to a different folder (manual protocol)

The launcher GUI does not yet offer "change project path". Until it does, a
move is a MANUAL protocol — follow it exactly; improvised moves lose KG
routing or leak VCO files into commits. Project identity (id, Weaviate
collections, secrets scoping) is keyed by the launcher DB row, NOT the path —
so a correct move changes only path-bearing state and never re-embeds
anything.

1. **Inventory first**: list what exists in BOTH the old and new folder.
   Files present on both sides with DIFFERENT content are conflicts — never
   auto-overwrite either side; merge deliberately (a project's live
   `.claude/CONTEXT_STATE.md` always beats a template seed).
2. **Copy additively** (`rsync -a --ignore-existing`): `.claude/`, root
   `CLAUDE.md`, `MEMORY.md`, `.env.vco.reference`, `.vscode/`,
   `infrastructure/`, `knowledge/` — existing destination files are never
   overwritten.
3. **Rewrite path-bearing values** in the destination: `KG_BASE_DIR` in
   `.claude/settings.json` and `.claude/env`, AND the deferral ledger's
   apply commands (`.claude/context/UPDATE_DEFERRED.md` + `.json` embed
   absolute paths — a stale `source <old>/.claude/env` would poison a
   session). Grep the old path across the whole destination afterwards —
   zero hits required.
4. **Git hygiene** (if the destination is a repo): add the bundle paths to
   `.git/info/exclude` (LOCAL-only, never the tracked `.gitignore`) so
   VCO-managed files can't reach a commit by accident; deliberately
   un-exclude anything you want tracked.
5. **Flip the DB row with the launcher CLOSED** (single-writer): back up
   `launcher.db`, then `UPDATE projects SET folder_path='<new>' WHERE
   id='<project-id>'`, then sweep EVERY table's path-like columns for the
   old path and CLASSIFY each hit: operational columns (rows future code
   acts on — `project_agents.file_path` and `project_skills.file_path`
   carry absolute paths) get rewritten in the same launcher-closed window;
   historical columns (`log_tail`, telemetry payloads) were TRUE at event
   time — leave them untouched, never falsify history. `PRAGMA
   wal_checkpoint(TRUNCATE)` when done. Note: harness per-path state
   (`~/.claude.json` project entry, `~/.claude/projects/<path-slug>/`
   auto-memory + transcripts) does NOT follow a move — COPY (never move)
   the auto-memory directory to the new path's slug if the old path hosted
   sessions.
6. **Re-point the toolchain**: relaunch the launcher; verify the hub resolves
   the new path (`/api/v1/projects/by-path`). Then run kg-sync from the new
   root WITH THE PROJECT'S OWN ENV and the VCO venv — a bare `kg-sync --all` can
   resolve the project's own `.venv` (no weaviate) or inherit another
   session's KG env:
   `cd <new-root> && set -a && source .claude/env && set +a && \
    <vco-venv>/bin/python .claude/scripts/sync_knowledge_graph.py --all`
   (content-identical nodes keep their embeddings; only file_path metadata
   refreshes). Re-run the code-graph analyzer on the new root when
   convenient.
7. **Never delete the old folder automatically** — leave it until a human
   confirms nothing was missed.
8. **Check `.mcp.json` at the destination.** A project-scoped `.mcp.json`
   (Anthropic's own config, often committed to the repo) takes PRECEDENCE
   over `.claude/settings.json` for MCP env. A checkout you adopt may carry
   its previous author's values — a different Weaviate URL, a foreign
   `KG_COLLECTION`, no shared-KG entry — and every KG search then runs
   against the wrong endpoint with no error. VCO detects and quarantines a
   contradicting `weaviate-kg` block (backing the file up first), but check
   it yourself when adopting an unfamiliar checkout. Restart Claude Code
   afterwards so the MCP re-reads the corrected env.
9. **After the move, re-read the deferral ledger with suspicion.** Before
   v0.2.92, some VCO checks re-derived the project's identity from the FOLDER
   BASENAME rather than the registered name, so a move could make a project's
   own live collections look like foreign "legacy" data — complete with drop
   commands. Identity now resolves from the registered row and the live
   bindings, and an emitted drop command re-validates against those bindings
   before it runs. A ledger entry written by an OLDER version can still carry
   a command built on the old, wrong identity. So before running ANY
   collection migration or drop command from
   `UPDATE_DEFERRED.md`, verify against the live bindings: the launcher's
   Identity tab, the hub's `/config` response, and the collections that
   actually hold your objects. If the "legacy" class is the one your
   project is reading, the detector is wrong, not your data.

